The asymptotic global condition number $K^+_{\infty}(t)$ is unrelated to the worst asymptotic behavior of the condition numbers $K(t,y_0, \widehat{z}_0)$. In fact, in Figure \ref{KKoverline} we also see, for each $\tau\in\{10,20,30,40\}$,  the condition number $K(t,y_{0\tau},\widehat{z}_{0\tau})$ (black solid lines) for an initial value $y_{0\tau}$ and a direction of perturbation $\widehat{z}_{0\tau}$ such that $K(\tau,y_{0\tau},\widehat{z}_{0\tau})=K(\tau)$. To obtain this, we take the initial value $y_{0\tau}$ such that
