\textbf{Returning collected list}. Cypher uses \texttt{COLLECT()} clause to
create list, in which the rows are defined inside the clause. We model
\texttt{COLLECT()} in the \texttt{RETURN} clause as function $collect(t,i)$ on
the columns of arbitrary tuple in the query result, which outputs 1 if the
$i$-th column of $t$ is collected and 0 otherwise. For example, we model
\texttt{RETURN COLLECT(x1.name)} as $[t.col_1=e_1.name]\times collect(t,1)$.

