\textcircled{2} \textbf{Eliminating undirected relationship pattern}.
Relationships in property graphs are directed. However, Cypher allows for
specifying undirected relationships to match relationships in both directions.
For example, \texttt{(a)-[]-(b)} represents both directions of relationship
patterns between node patterns \texttt{(a)} and \texttt{(b)}, i.e.,
\texttt{(a)-[]->(b)} and \texttt{(a)<-[]-(b)}. As shown in
\tabref{tab:normalized}, we transform undirected relationship patterns using the
\texttt{UNION ALL} clause to combine both directions into two subqueries.

