The input diffusion timestep $k$, heightmap $\rvh$, target direction $\rvd$, and noisy frames $\rvx_k$ are first encoded using different embedding networks to map each into tokens for the transformer.
The heightmap observations are processed with a convolutional neural network, and the image patches are extracted and processed into tokens by an MLP. 
