\item[]{\em Nature of problem:} Analytic computations in quantum field theory often produce large expressions involving complicated rational functions. In many cases, such as symbolic integration, performing partial fraction decomposition of the latter is vital. Even though univariate partial fraction decomposition is conceptually well-understood, the complexity of state-of-the-art calculations is such that use of readily available tools, such as the {\tt Apart} command in {\sc Mathematica}, becomes highly impractical due to time and memory constraints. Here we present {\tt LinApart}, a routine developed for performing univariate partial fraction decomposition in a highly efficient manner. Improvements in timing and memory usage of up to five orders of magnitude are achieved for rational expressions with as few as ten denominator factors. As such, the routine allows to perform decomposition problems that were previously intractable.

\item[]{\em Solution method:} The {\tt LinApart} routine implements a simple closed form expression for univariate partial fraction decomposition of rational functions with fully factored denominators based on the residue theorem. The {\sc Mathematica} implementation makes use of the highly efficient built-in differentiation routine to evaluate this formula. The {\sc C} language implementation employs a version of the formula that does not require symbolic differentiation but is rather based on the computation of multinomial coefficients. 

