\subsubsection{Activity initialisations}
\label{activity-inits}
Here we present some additional results on the initialisation of the activities of a PCN. All experiments used fully connected ResNets, GD as activity optimiser, and as many inference steps as the number of hidden layers. For intuition, we start with linear scalar PCNs or chains. First, we verify that the ill-conditioning of the inference landscape (\S \ref{ill-cond-infer}) causes the activities to barely move during inference, and increasing the activity learning rate leads to divergence for both forward and random initialisation (Fig. \ref{fig:sp-activity-inits}). Similar results are observed for $\mu$PC (see Fig. \ref{fig:mupc-activity-inits}).
