To see that $G_k$ is a minor of $F_k$ it is enough to contract, for every $1 \le i \le 2k$, vertex $v_{i,2k}$ with vertices of paths $Z_i$ and $W_i$. Since taking a minor does not increase the treewidth, we obtain the following corollary.

