	In this subsection, we assume that $\G$ is a ring graph, with each node having a self-loop. The weight matrix $W$ is a symmetric circulant matrix, and has the following form for odd and even number of agents.
	\begin{itemize}
		\item[(a)] \textbf{Odd}. If $n=2s-1$ for some $s>1$, $W=C(w_0,w_1,\dots,w_{s-1},w_{s-1},\dots,w_1)$, with $w_0, w_1>0$, and $w_0+2\sum_{\ell=1}^{s-1}w_\ell=1$;
