			\item as $\theta$ grows, the solution becomes agent $1$ for small $\omega$ and $3$ for large $\omega$. In particular, for $\theta=0.99$, the solution changes when $\omega$ changes from $0.15$ to $0.18$. Note that for $\omega=0.15$, it holds $g_3=1.25<1.2565=g_3$, and for $\omega=0.18$, it holds $g_1=1.2298<1.25=g_3$. Therefore, Proposition \ref{prop:big_stub} is validated.
		\end{itemize}
