\subsection{Model framework}\label{sec:framework}

A lightweight, MATLAB-based solver and visualization tool \footnote{\url{https://github.com/RRZE-HPC/OSC-AD}} was designed to explore the dynamics of MPI-parallel, bulk-synchronous and barrier-free applications modeled as coupled oscillators. The framework supports multiple communication topologies -- including open chains, rings, meshes, and random graphs -- and allows adjustable boundary conditions and interaction potentials.

By tuning model parameters such as coupling strength, noise, and communication delay, the framework enables investigation of key performance phenomena including synchronization, idle wave propagation, bottleneck amplification, and symmetry-breaking effects. 
