We will see that certain algebraic properties of the semiautomaton and the query imply that we have to fall in one of these cases. For example, if the query is commutative (Appendix ~\ref{sec:commutative}), then free termination falls in the first scenario, while if the semiautomaton forms a group structure this means that no free termination state exists (Section ~\ref{sec:groups}).
