\section{Introduction}
The idea of ``Windbreaking-as-a-Service" (WaaS) is to offer a low-tech platooning solution for everyone. On a dedicated platform, not unlike car-pooling, potential donors of wind shadow (``windbreakers") offer spots in their aerodynamic wake, such that other vehicles (``windsurfers") can occupy those spots and benefit from reduced aerodynamic drag and hence a reduced power consumption\cite{duoba2023empirical}. At this stage, we restrict ourselves to {\em pairs} of vehicles: on each portion of the trip, one windbreaker leads exactly one windsurfer (Fig. \ref{fig: windbreaking}). 
